test_command=sh tests/conventions_test.sh && sh tests/skills-activation-prompts_test.sh && sh tests/closingblock_test.sh && sh tests/readmefile_test.sh && sh tests/entities-operations-table_test.sh
id=conventions-01 result=green reason=unit test "conventions-01: the Specification Rules scenario-naming bullet defines the index as two zero-padded digits sequential from 01 while keeping the one-word feature rule, the tag-comment format, and the tag-description rule" (tests/conventions_test.sh) passes -- the bullet now states "<index>" is two zero-padded digits, sequential from 01 within the sub-spec (first <feature>-01, next <feature>-02, and so on) while the one-word <feature> rule, the tag-comment first-line format, and the no-other-ids-in-a-description rule survive verbatim
id=conventions-02 result=green reason=unit test "conventions-02: the End-To-End QA Suite first bullet states exactly one suite per change in the fixed file e2e-qa.feature, keeps the operating rules, and drops the One per feature wording" (tests/conventions_test.sh) passes -- the first bullet states exactly one end-to-end QA suite per change written to the fixed file `e2e-qa.feature` in the change directory (one per change, not one per feature), the UI/no-internal-API, affordances, and user-visible-workflow rules survive, and "One per feature" is gone from the section and the whole prompt
id=conventions-03 result=green reason=unit test "conventions-03: the Output relevant-files bullet states one section per sub-spec with relevant files and the declared kebab-case destination domain, names no README.md, and leaves the overview bullet byte-for-byte unchanged" (tests/conventions_test.sh) passes -- the bullet states one section per sub-spec in the overview file carrying relevant files (pointers only, not a code walkthrough) and the declared kebab-case destination domain, contains no "README.md" literal, the overview bullet is byte-for-byte unchanged vs HEAD, and the section states the fixed name exactly once (tests/readmefile_test.sh and tests/entities-operations-table_test.sh stay green unmodified)
id=conventions-04 result=green reason=unit tests "conventions-04: both suites carrying the specifier diff-window pins pass with the guards still registered, and print the loud notes while the rewording is uncommitted", "conventions-04: prompts-05's specifier guard retires by gating -- loud retirement note, additive-shape checks skipped -- when the fixture copy differs from HEAD", "conventions-04: prompts-05's byte-for-byte pin is still enforced quietly when the fixture copy is byte-identical to HEAD", "conventions-04: closingblock-05's two specifier diff-window assertions retire by gating with two loud notes when the fixture copy differs from HEAD", "conventions-04: closingblock-05's specifier assertions stay enforced quietly when the fixture copy is byte-identical to HEAD", and "conventions-04: closingblock-05's degenerate no-diff state check is kept -- a committed prompt without the closing-block bullet still fails it, with no note" (tests/conventions_test.sh) pass against throwaway git fixtures -- prompts-05's specifier guard prints a loud retirement note and skips the closingblock-era additive-shape checks when the copy differs from HEAD (guard stays registered) and still enforces the byte-for-byte pin when identical; both closingblock-05 diff-window assertions retire by gating the same way with their own loud notes while the degenerate no-diff state check is kept and still bites; every other assertion of both suites (orchestrator-prose diff-shape gate, no-role-level-##-Skills boundary, closing-block vocabulary/report tests, byte-unchanged meta files) keeps passing -- full regression: all 24 tests/*_test.sh suites green
